+## Vault mode
+
+Check this first. When vault mode is on, it replaces the prereq and output-file steps below.
+
+- **requirements-grill.** If `.planner.yaml` exists at the repo root, vault mode is on. A `CAP-NNN` scope is required instead of a slug; if the user gave none, ask for one. Read `.claude/skills/planner/references/REQUIREMENTS-IN-VAULT.md` and follow it. If that file is missing, stop: *"This repo is an initiative vault, but the planner plugin is not installed at `.claude/skills/planner`. Install it before running requirements-grill here."*
+- **tech-design-grill.** If the user passed `--vault <path> --app <APP-id>`, vault mode is on. The prereq is the app's building-blocks page in `<path>` carrying a `handed_off:` field, instead of `docs/requirements/<slug>.md`. If the page or the field is missing, stop: *"`<APP-id>` has no `handed_off` field in that vault, so its pages are not handed over yet. Ask the solution lead to hand it off first."* Then read `<path>/.claude/skills/planner/references/TECH-DESIGN-FROM-VAULT.md` and follow it. If that file is missing, stop and say the planner plugin in that vault is too old.
+
+Without either, run the steps below as written.
